From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:33:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: Restore DCP address cells for J713
 IOMMU validation

The DART handoff validator checks address and size cell counts for every
owner in an iommu-addresses tuple, including the DCP PIODMA child. Without
cell counts on its DCP parent, of_n_addr_cells() and of_n_size_cells() warn
before falling back to the SoC node. This taints the kernel during boot.

Restore the two-cell address and size declarations on the shared J713/J715
DCP node so the inherited IOMMU tuples have explicit parent cell counts.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit c9c212631fb35881170a6029683d9d577e1513cb)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-j715.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-j715.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-j715.dtsi
index 62207f9f63..0fa670f5eb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-j715.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-j715.dtsi
@@ -135,6 +135,8 @@ &ps_gfx {
 &dcp {
 	apple,panel-width-mm = <290>;
 	apple,panel-height-mm = <188>;
+	#address-cells = <2>;
+	#size-cells = <2>;
 };
 
 /* The enclave must take the sleep request, so its driver has to bind. */
-- 
